WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.470 --> 00:00:15.791
Summer was coming to an end.

2
00:00:17.632 --> 00:00:19.994
Townspeople continued to gather at the statue.

3
00:00:21.534 --> 00:00:22.855
Some came to admire it.

4
00:00:24.196 --> 00:00:25.757
Others enjoyed its smile.

5
00:00:28.018 --> 00:00:31.300
But most still came to talk about their problems.

6
00:00:33.528 --> 00:00:35.730
The statue listened to everything they said.

7
00:00:36.771 --> 00:00:39.113
Hearing people's problems every day was hard.

8
00:00:40.515 --> 00:00:42.697
And it was making him sad.

9
00:00:45.940 --> 00:00:49.443
Even compliments about his beauty couldn't make him happy anymore.

10
00:00:49.463 --> 00:00:55.169
"I never knew life was so hard," he thought.

11
00:00:55.189 --> 00:00:57.271
"But now I do.

12
00:00:59.464 --> 00:01:05.509
If only I could stop smiling, I could show people that I'm listening to their pain.

13
00:01:07.070 --> 00:01:11.113
But like my heart, my smile is made of heavy stone."

14
00:01:13.555 --> 00:01:16.257
A few days later, Swallow flew over the town.

15
00:01:17.838 --> 00:01:20.260
He was looking for a gift to bring to his love.

16
00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:25.344
"I want something as beautiful as she is," he thought.

17
00:01:27.348 --> 00:01:29.890
He spotted some daisies down on a hilltop.

18
00:01:31.551 --> 00:01:33.132
But they had begun to wilt.

19
00:01:36.614 --> 00:01:39.635
So Swallow flew on until he saw an apple orchard.

20
00:01:39.655 --> 00:01:44.518
"I'll bring her a bright red apple," he thought.

21
00:01:46.199 --> 00:01:47.940
But none of the apples looked right.

22
00:01:51.262 --> 00:01:54.064
At last, Swallow spotted the perfect thing.

23
00:01:55.100 --> 00:01:57.962
A rosebush was growing under a statue.

24
00:01:57.982 --> 00:02:01.725
"Hooray!" Swallow cheered.

25
00:02:01.745 --> 00:02:05.187
"I'll pick the most perfect rose!"

26
00:02:07.108 --> 00:02:09.110
Swallow swooped toward the rosebush.

27
00:02:10.611 --> 00:02:14.373
But as he flew past the statue, something flashed in his eye.

28
00:02:15.554 --> 00:02:19.036
It was the statue's gold, gleaming brightly in the sun.

29
00:02:20.397 --> 00:02:23.960
Its three jewels sparkled like stars at night.

30
00:02:25.976 --> 00:02:28.118
Swallow gasped at its beauty.

31
00:02:28.138 --> 00:02:32.321
"This statue would be the finest gift for my love.

32
00:02:33.722 --> 00:02:35.363
If only it wasn't so big and heavy!

33
00:02:36.924 --> 00:02:37.264
Oh well.

34
00:02:37.524 --> 00:02:38.745
A perfect rose will do."

35
00:02:40.566 --> 00:02:43.969
Swallow continued toward the roses when he heard a moan.

36
00:02:46.630 --> 00:02:49.352
He looked around but didn't see anyone.

37
00:02:49.372 --> 00:02:52.214
"Who's there?"

38
00:02:53.555 --> 00:02:54.376
No one answered.

39
00:02:55.520 --> 00:02:56.761
There was another moan.

40
00:03:01.385 --> 00:03:04.107
It sounded like it was coming from the statue.

41
00:03:04.127 --> 00:03:09.651
"It couldn't be the statue," Swallow thought.

42
00:03:09.671 --> 00:03:11.613
"It looks so happy.

43
00:03:12.533 --> 00:03:14.755
And nothing that beautiful could ever be sad.

44
00:03:16.296 --> 00:03:18.198
Besides, statues don't talk.

45
00:03:18.478 --> 00:03:18.838
Do they?

46
00:03:20.139 --> 00:03:20.980
It must have been the wind."

47
00:03:24.208 --> 00:03:28.752
Swallow started looking for the best rose when his flock landed nearby.

48
00:03:28.772 --> 00:03:34.437
"Swallow! Come along," Leader called.

49
00:03:34.457 --> 00:03:37.779
"It's time to fly to Egypt."

50
00:03:37.800 --> 00:03:41.823
"Have a good trip," Swallow said.

51
00:03:41.843 --> 00:03:44.785
"I'm staying here, near my love."

52
00:03:46.827 --> 00:03:47.848
Leader frowned.

53
00:03:47.868 --> 00:03:50.390
"Winter is coming.

54
00:03:51.291 --> 00:03:52.452
You'll freeze."

55
00:03:54.672 --> 00:03:57.615
"I have my love to keep me warm," Swallow said.

56
00:03:57.635 --> 00:04:01.860
"You're making a mistake," Leader said.

57
00:04:01.880 --> 00:04:08.567
"But if you insist, then I wish you good luck."

58
00:04:08.587 --> 00:04:09.468
"I won't need it!"

59
00:04:09.909 --> 00:04:12.752
Swallow said as the flock flew away.
